{"title":"2011 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 17","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(Quick,_Non-Rigorous_Trends)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (Quick, Non-Rigorous Trends)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_17&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/e/78e38944bebb9f5bca9de1730b7a8b8d5f414447.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x) = 10^{10x}, g(x) = \\log_{10}\\left(\\frac{x}{10}\\right), h_1(x) = g(f(x))$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"384\" height=\"34\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/d/bad508d497ff0fadd24121a96bdce0693162f7c5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$h_n(x) = h_1(h_{n-1}(x))$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"160\" height=\"18\" /> for integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/2/2/72287b09043ed45b372a517d764e12d07aff8071.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\geq 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"14\" />. What is the sum of the digits of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/6/3/863fe953862a8b58da96f0031d832907fb5b21f4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$h_{2011}(1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"59\" height=\"18\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/e/3/7e32ba9c94508a9381a3ef57f849fc8b28eb40a1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 16081 \\qquad \\textbf{(B)}\\ 16089 \\qquad \\textbf{(C)}\\ 18089 \\qquad \\textbf{(D)}\\ 18098 \\qquad \\textbf{(E)}\\ 18099$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"530\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_17&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/0/b808e260d341f190e2080beaa349f1f7bba735c5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g(x)=\\log_{10}\\left(\\frac{x}{10}\\right)=\\log_{10}\\left({x}\\right) - 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"261\" height=\"34\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/2/13244fc0b6d1bca12e6688b2f31d4af1fbfbf728.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$h_{1}(x)=g(f(x))\\text{ = }g(10^{10x})=\\log_{10}\\left({10^{10x}}\\right){ - 1 = 10x - 1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -7px\" width=\"446\" height=\"23\" />\n</p><p>Proof by induction that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/d/7ad7d21b936cfbfbeb9364366974d12b2652eb3c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$h_{n}(x)\\text{ = }10^n x - (1 + 10 + 10^2 + ... + 10^{n-1})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"341\" height=\"19\" />:\n</p><p>For <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/9/1d96ecc15129c5631ba4a2c6578e91e3d13e3baf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/2/5121ef08cd68c0c0ff2c84566093ea03702c9c6d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$h_{1}(x)=10x - 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"125\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>Assume <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/3/b/53b06cd01df9c57797e532df89787689643f7448.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$h_{n}(x)=10^n x - (1 + 10 + 10^2 + ... + 10^{n-1})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"342\" height=\"19\" /> is true for n:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/b/d1b65beafdbc573de32fba46940e6969122aa0df.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} h_{n+1}(x)&amp;= h_{1}(h_{n}(x))\\\\ &amp;=10 h_{n}(x) - 1\\\\ &amp;=10 (10^n x   - (1 + 10 + 10^2 + ... + 10^{n-1})) - 1\\\\ &amp;= 10^{n+1} x - (10 + 10^2 + ... + 10^{n}) - 1\\\\ &amp;= 10^{n+1} x - (1 + 10 + 10^2 + ... + 10^{(n+1)-1}) \\end{align*}\" width=\"422\" height=\"127\" />\n</p><p>Therefore, if it is true for n, then it is true for n+1; since it is also true for n = 1, it is true for all positive integers n.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/7/8/d78b2be433c30d189e4d9a1f550d0772c1dc2d94.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$h_{2011}(1) = 10^{2011}\\times 1{ - }(1 + 10 + 10^2 + ... + 10^{2010})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"391\" height=\"19\" />, which is the 2011-digit number 8888...8889\n</p><p>The sum of the digits is 8 times 2010 plus 9, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/e/b5e7c029728fcb1e1ea88a359398f79971230bb1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{16089\\textbf{(B)}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"85\" height=\"28\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28Quick.2C_Non-Rigorous_Trends.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(Quick,_Non-Rigorous_Trends)\">Solution 2 (Quick, Non-Rigorous Trends)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_17&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (Quick, Non-Rigorous Trends)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>As before, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/9/5/d95f07887004d3c4861237a74deafe8bd2b51635.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$h_1(x)=10x-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"125\" height=\"18\" />. Compute <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/e/8fea77f751d8481a71f528a0c0a0f9aafa92059a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$h_1(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"41\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/3/3231174cb0fa5800a1e168e5c200699d95ed924c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$h_2(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"41\" height=\"18\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/a/54a9a6122fc2682fb4605342f14e2b59b66a69e4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$h_3(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"41\" height=\"18\" /> to yield 9, 89, and 889. Notice how this trend will repeat this trend (multiply by 10, subtract 1, repeat). As such, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/6/876f9a67b238e4b76a98886981fbf0368ce8e5a5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$h_{2011}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"35\" height=\"15\" /> is just 2010 8's followed by a nine. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/c/9/5c9c59367d18357b7b856924fc3fbb7612e57862.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2010(8)+9=\\boxed{\\textbf{B)}16089}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"193\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p><p>~~BJHHar\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_17&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"2\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_12B\" title=\"2011 AMC 12B\">2011 AMC 12B</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_12B_Problems\" title=\"2011 AMC 12B Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_12B_Answer_Key\" title=\"2011 AMC 12B Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_16\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2011 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 16\">Problem 16</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_18\" title=\"2011 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 18\">Problem 18</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2011 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2011 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2011 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2011 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2011 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2011 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2011 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <